"""OpenFE SepTop workflow page for ChemFlow Studio — the separated-topologies
relative-BFE setup, driving the ``alchemforge openfe septop`` CLI.

SepTop is a RELATIVE method: two ligands A and B are perturbed at once (A coupled
while B is decoupled, and vice versa), so every lambda column is an ``_A`` / ``_B``
pair. It plans a perturbation network like RBFE but has NO per-edge atom mapping
(separated topologies) — the planner only uses a mapper internally to score
candidate edges. It uses a host restraint like ABFE.

Sub-tabs: Ligand Prep (charge) → Network (planner; no mapping) → System (soluble
or membrane) → Restraints → FEP simulation (dual A/B lambda schedules, buildable
from a function) → Job (HPC) → Execution.
"""

